**Issue**: #420
**Date**: 2026-09-24
**Status**: Approved
**Author**: NMG

Feature: Wait for exact host review receipts before closing sibling panes
  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Every sibling settles before any receipt inspection or pane close
    Given three concurrently launched reviewers have distinct exact assignments
    And agentWait returns while a second reviewer is still working
    When execute collects review results
    Then it continues observing the working reviewer until idle or done without a settlement deadline
    And it awaits all three workers before inspecting the first host receipt
    And it closes no review pane while a sibling remains unsettled
    And idle or done state alone is not accepted as a final review result

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Delayed host append becomes durable within the bounded window
    Given all review siblings have settled and one assignment-bound host JSONL lacks a final result
    And the host appends a partial JSONL line before completing a valid final review_result after multiple one-second observation pauses
    When execute re-inspects that same receipt within 30 pauses
    Then it uses only the completed host result with its exact assignment
    And it publishes the existing aggregate artifact and handoff only after all sibling host results validate
    And only then does it close the sibling panes

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario Outline: Unproven receipt evidence cannot spend review recovery
    Given all review siblings have settled
    And one required host receipt path has <condition> through its bounded observation
    When execute cannot validate every nonempty review_result
    Then review fails without an aggregate artifact or review handoff
    And all review panes, assignments, and receipt artifacts remain for diagnosis
    And it does not consume invalid_review_slice recovery or launch a replacement
    And no terminal prose is substituted for host evidence

    Examples:
      | condition                            |
      | no final review_result               |
      | a persistently malformed JSONL line |
      | a foreign receipt                    |
      | a wrong-assignment digest            |
      | an empty delimited review result     |

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: Receipt arriving after the bound is too late
    Given every reviewer is idle or done but one valid final host result remains absent for 30 one-second receipt observation pauses
    When the receipt observation limit is reached
    Then execute fails without accepting a later terminal message
    And it leaves all review panes and evidence intact without an artifact or review handoff
    And it does not consume invalid_review_slice recovery

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: Review findings preserve their meaning
    Given every sibling has settled and every exact host result is valid and nonempty
    And one result contains review findings while another says "No findings."
    When execute completes review collection
    Then the existing aggregation retains the findings without treating them as a missing receipt
    And pane closure occurs only after every required receipt has validated

  @SCN006 @regression
  Scenario: Proven prohibited access consumes one whole-stage replacement
    Given every sibling has settled and its exact host receipt has a complete nonempty review_result
    And a host receipt proves prohibited access on one original slice
    And the bound review owner has an unconsumed invalid_review_slice allowance
    When execute handles the contaminated review stage
    Then it preserves the original review evidence and consumes exactly one owner-bound whole-stage replacement
    And it relaunches the review stage once rather than just the contaminated slice
    And only valid replacement receipts can produce the successful aggregate handoff

  @SCN007 @regression
  Scenario Outline: A replacement failure cannot replenish review recovery
    Given proven prohibited access consumed the one owner-bound whole-stage replacement
    When <replacement outcome> occurs
    Then execute stops without a third review attempt or replenished allowance
    And the original review evidence remains intact

    Examples:
      | replacement outcome                  |
      | a second proven contamination       |
      | a failed replacement worker         |
      | a missing replacement review_result |

  @SCN008 @regression
  Scenario: No valid owner or consumed allowance prevents replacement
    Given an exact host receipt proves prohibited access with a complete nonempty review_result
    And the review owner is absent, changed, or has already consumed its allowance
    When execute evaluates invalid_review_slice recovery
    Then it fails without launching another review attempt
    And it preserves the original review evidence

  @SCN009 @regression
  Scenario: Worker failure is not receipt quiescence or contamination
    Given a sibling worker fails before all reviewers become idle or done
    When execute observes the failed worker
    Then it stops before reading any host receipt or closing any review pane
    And it retains all panes and evidence without an aggregate artifact or handoff
    And it consumes no invalid_review_slice recovery or replacement
